{
  "key": "water-utility",
  "name": "Municipal Water Utility",
  "category": "mixed",
  "description": "A municipal water / wastewater utility seen from the HQ core SPAN: corporate IT, an IT/OT DMZ (historian replica, jump host), the SCADA operations LAN (AVEVA-style SCADA pair, historian, engineering WS), the treatment-plant cell (Rockwell CompactLogix + PowerFlex high-service pumps, Modicon M580 chemical feed with Danfoss VFDs, Hach chlorine/turbidity analyzers) and eight remote lift/booster stations behind cellular modems (Sierra Wireless, Digi, Moxa) on the SCADA WAN. Station RTUs (SCADAPack) sit behind each modem's NAT, so HQ sees them as the modem's WAN address; SCADA polls them over DNP3 / Modbus every 1-2 min with heavy jitter. Planted findings: an unauthenticated VNC HMI at LS04, cleartext Telnet to the LS07 modem, default SNMP community on every modem, an EOL Windows XP filter HMI, an EOL SCADAPack 334E. Run: tgt run --env water-utility --pcap water.pcap --once --rate 0",
